{
  "version": 3,
  "created": "2026-09-05",
  "corpus_version": "LEGAL_KB_V1_GOLD",
  "notes": [
    "Drawn from query classes the hardcoded heuristics were never tuned against. Anything the LOW_SCORE_FALLBACK_TERMS phrase ('non-cognizable offence General Diary entry SOP complaint procedure'), the PROCEDURE_ANCHOR_TERMS list, or the missing-item regex in the drafting agent was written for is excluded: FIR registration, complaint procedure, General Diary entries, non-cognizable offences and 'my X went missing'. Those queries measure the heuristics, not retrieval.",
    "Relevance is expressed against Acts, section numbers and distinctive phrases, never chunk IDs. Chunk IDs are content-addressed and change on every re-chunk, which is precisely when this set is needed.",
    "Every answerable item was checked against the corpus on disk before being written, so a miss here is a retrieval failure and not a missing document.",
    "Expected abstentions are scored alongside answerable questions, and false abstention is scored too. Tightening the gate without measuring the cost looks free otherwise.",
    "Roles are recorded because police and advocate ask differently shaped questions than citizens, and a set drawn only from citizen phrasing would tune retrieval to one of the three.",
    "v3.1 widens the police slice from 12 to 25 items. Twelve was too few to tune against: a single item moved police recall by 0.08, which is larger than most of the changes being measured."
  ],
